Problem Statement:
Project Title:

Hospital Bed Availability Tracking System

Problem:

Hospitals often need to manage a large number of beds across different wards such as General, ICU, Emergency, and Private rooms. When bed information is maintained manually or updated slowly, staff may have difficulty knowing which beds are currently available, occupied, reserved, or under maintenance.

This can lead to:

Delay in assigning beds
Difficulty tracking vacant beds
Manual errors
Poor coordination between departments
Difficulty monitoring ICU and emergency bed availability
Proposed Solution

The Hospital Bed Availability Tracking System is a software application that maintains the current status of hospital beds in a centralized system.

The system allows authorized hospital staff to:

Add and manage hospital beds
View available beds
Update bed status
Assign beds to patients
Release beds when patients are discharged
Track beds by ward/type
Search for available beds
View bed availability statistics
Main Objective

To develop a system that provides accurate and up-to-date information about hospital bed availability and helps hospital staff efficiently manage bed allocation.